; ============================================================================
; Step 11 GDL-I fragment: + TINY ENDGAME RULE — FINAL STEP.
;
; Builds on step 10. Adds the v2 tiny-endgame loss condition.
; Per RULEBOOK_v2.md (Tiny Endgame Rule):
;
;   Activation: the rule applies when ALL of:
;     - No pawns remain on the board.
;     - 6 or fewer non-king non-neutral pieces (boulder excluded,
;       kings ignored).
;     - The position BALANCES under the cancel-queens + 1-to-2
;       valuation.
;
;   Distance counts: for each royal distance 1..14, keep a count
;   of how many times that distance has occurred while the rule
;   is active. Activation sets the current royal distance count
;   to 1. After each non-capture turn, increment by 1. After a
;   capture, reset all counts to 0 then set the current
;   distance's count to 1 if the rule still applies.
;
;   Limit: a player may not make a NON-CAPTURE turn that would
;   cause the resulting royal distance's count to exceed 3. If
;   every legal turn would do so, that player loses.
;
; This is the FINAL step of the 11-step rollout. After it, the
; fragment series matches the full v2 ruleset modulo
; implementation simplifications documented per step.
;
; STATUS (issue #389). The LIMIT is complete: `legal` itself is filtered
; by each turn's resulting royal distance (tiny_endgame_forbids, guarded
; on every move / transform / manipulate legal rule in steps 1-9), and
; the non-capture count update is complete. Both are cross-validated
; against the engine by tests/test_gdl_tiny_endgame_filter.py. Still a
; SKETCH: ACTIVATION (counts_at_least_7 and
; cancel_queens_valuation_balanced are undefined, so
; tiny_endgame_position never holds) and, resting on it, the first
; activation and the re-initialisation after a capture. In play the
; rule is therefore switched on only by an injected state carrying
; (tiny_endgame_active) and its distance_count facts.
; ============================================================================

(role white)
(role black)

; (init facts and helpers from steps 1-10 carry over.)

; ---- Tiny-endgame activation ------------------------------------------

(<= (pawnless)
    (not (any_pawn)))
(<= (any_pawn)
    (true (cell ?f ?r ?c pawn)))

; non-king non-boulder piece count: defined recursively, capped
; at the activation threshold (≤ 6).
(<= (non_king_non_boulder_count_at_most 6)
    ; Counting predicate would enumerate every non-king non-
    ; boulder piece and check |set| ≤ 6. In GDL-I this is
    ; expressible via a counter-like recursion but is verbose.
    ; Sketched: at_most_6 means there is NO 7-element set of
    ; distinct non-king non-boulder pieces.
    (not (at_least_7_non_king_non_boulder)))

(<= (at_least_7_non_king_non_boulder)
    ; A 7-piece existence check; encoded as 7 distinct cell
    ; facts. (Spelled out for clarity rather than via a recursive
    ; counter — GDL-I doesn't have arithmetic; we just guard
    ; the activation predicate.)
    ; The detailed 7-cell enumeration would be a long disjunction
    ; — we sketch with a placeholder predicate.
    (counts_at_least_7))

; Balance predicate: cancel-queens + 1-to-2 valuation.
; (Detailed encoding requires arithmetic up to ~6. Sketched as
; a `(tiny_balanced)` predicate that the reasoner-integration
; phase will expand. The rulebook section gives the precise
; numerical condition:
;   If r >= 1: balanced iff r <= N_L - N_M <= 2r.
;   If r = 0: balanced iff N_M = N_L.)
(<= (tiny_balanced)
    (cancel_queens_valuation_balanced))

; ---- Activation: TWO distinct concepts, deliberately named apart -----
;
; The engine keeps these separate and the GDL previously conflated them
; under one name, which is why every rule below was unreachable.
;
;   tiny_endgame_position  DERIVED. "Does the position qualify right
;                          now?" -- recomputed every turn. This is
;                          Board.is_tiny_endgame().
;
;   tiny_endgame_active    FLUENT. "Have we already started counting?"
;                          -- remembered across turns. This is
;                          Board.tiny_endgame_active.
;
; The distinction is load-bearing. Activation RESETS the distance
; counts (Board.init_tiny_endgame), so it must happen exactly once, on
; the turn the position first qualifies. If it re-fired every turn the
; counts would reset to 1 forever, never reach the limit of 3, and the
; rule would never do anything.
;
; Previously `tiny_endgame_active` was defined as a derived rule but
; read everywhere as `(true (tiny_endgame_active))`, and no `next` rule
; ever wrote it -- so the fluent was permanently false and the entire
; tiny-endgame rule was dead. (Issue #177 B4.)

(<= (tiny_endgame_position)
    (pawnless)
    (non_king_non_boulder_count_at_most 6)
    (tiny_balanced))

; ---- The turn being made ------------------------------------------------
;
; Only the player in control makes a turn; the other role plays noop.
; Every rule below that looks at "this turn" reads it through
; turn_made, so the noop is never mistaken for a non-capture turn.

(<= (turn_made ?move)
    (true (control ?player))
    (does ?player ?move))

; ---- Activation flag ----------------------------------------------------
;
; First activation: the position qualifies and we were not already
; counting. (SKETCH: tiny_endgame_position rests on the undefined
; counts_at_least_7 and cancel_queens_valuation_balanced above, and it
; is read in the state BEFORE the turn, where the rulebook measures the
; position after it. Issue #389 leaves activation for a later change.)
(<= (next (tiny_endgame_active))
    (tiny_endgame_position)
    (not (true (tiny_endgame_active))))

; Once counting, a non-capture turn never ends the rule: the pieces are
; the same, so the position still qualifies. This is
; Board.update_distance_count(captured=False), which leaves the flag
; set. (It used to require tiny_endgame_position, which is undefined,
; so the flag died after one turn and the counts with it.)
(<= (next (tiny_endgame_active))
    (true (tiny_endgame_active))
    (not_a_capture_turn))

; After a capture the rule stays on only if the position still
; qualifies. (SKETCH, as above: read before the turn, not after it.)
(<= (next (tiny_endgame_active))
    (true (tiny_endgame_active))
    (a_capture_turn)
    (tiny_endgame_position))

; `was_active_last_turn` is simply the flag as it stands BEFORE this
; turn's update -- previously undefined, which made `just_activated`
; degenerate (negation-as-failure on an undefined predicate always
; succeeds).
(<= (was_active_last_turn)
    (true (tiny_endgame_active)))

; ---- Royal distance -----------------------------------------------------
;
; RULEBOOK: "Royal distance: the Manhattan distance between the
; closest pair of opposing royal pieces." A royal piece is a king or
; the royal queen, in ANY form: a transformed royal queen is still a
; queen cell carrying queen_royal.

(<= (royal_at ?owner ?f ?r)
    (true (cell ?f ?r ?owner king)))
(<= (royal_at ?owner ?f ?r)
    (true (cell ?f ?r ?owner queen))
    (true (queen_royal ?f ?r)))

; Small arithmetic for distances 0..14. Kept apart from `succ`, which
; also drives turn_number, so the distance rules do not change how far
; the turn counter runs.
(<= (distance_succ 0 1)) (<= (distance_succ 1 2)) (<= (distance_succ 2 3))
(<= (distance_succ 3 4)) (<= (distance_succ 4 5)) (<= (distance_succ 5 6))
(<= (distance_succ 6 7)) (<= (distance_succ 7 8)) (<= (distance_succ 8 9))
(<= (distance_succ 9 10)) (<= (distance_succ 10 11))
(<= (distance_succ 11 12)) (<= (distance_succ 12 13))
(<= (distance_succ 13 14))

(<= (distance_less ?a ?b)
    (distance_succ ?a ?b))
(<= (distance_less ?a ?c)
    (distance_succ ?a ?b)
    (distance_less ?b ?c))

; (distance_sum ?a ?b ?c): a + b = c. Called with ?a a file gap (0..7),
; so the base case's (distance_succ ?a ?n) always holds.
(<= (distance_sum ?a 0 ?a)
    (distance_succ ?a ?n))
(<= (distance_sum ?a ?b ?c)
    (distance_succ ?b0 ?b)
    (distance_sum ?a ?b0 ?c0)
    (distance_succ ?c0 ?c))

; Gaps between two files and between two ranks.
(<= (file_east_by ?f1 ?f2 1)
    (file_eastward ?f1 ?f2))
(<= (file_east_by ?f1 ?f2 ?n)
    (file_eastward ?f1 ?f3)
    (file_east_by ?f3 ?f2 ?m)
    (distance_succ ?m ?n))
(<= (file_gap ?f ?f 0)
    (file ?f))
(<= (file_gap ?f1 ?f2 ?n)
    (file_east_by ?f1 ?f2 ?n))
(<= (file_gap ?f1 ?f2 ?n)
    (file_east_by ?f2 ?f1 ?n))

(<= (rank_up_by ?r1 ?r2 1)
    (rank_upward ?r1 ?r2))
(<= (rank_up_by ?r1 ?r2 ?n)
    (rank_upward ?r1 ?r3)
    (rank_up_by ?r3 ?r2 ?m)
    (distance_succ ?m ?n))
(<= (rank_gap ?r ?r 0)
    (rank ?r))
(<= (rank_gap ?r1 ?r2 ?n)
    (rank_up_by ?r1 ?r2 ?n))
(<= (rank_gap ?r1 ?r2 ?n)
    (rank_up_by ?r2 ?r1 ?n))

(<= (manhattan ?f1 ?r1 ?f2 ?r2 ?d)
    (file_gap ?f1 ?f2 ?a)
    (rank_gap ?r1 ?r2 ?b)
    (distance_sum ?a ?b ?d))

; ---- Where the royals stand after a turn --------------------------------
;
; (turn_squares ?move ?from_f ?from_r ?to_f ?to_r ?gone_f ?gone_r): the
; piece the turn moves goes from ?from to ?to, and whatever stood on
; ?gone is removed. Only these turn types move a piece that can be
; royal; every other turn (transform, the boulder's first move,
; promotion) leaves every royal where it is.
;
; The manipulate case matters: a TRANSFORMED royal queen can be
; manipulated by the enemy queen, so the enemy's turn can move a royal
; and change the distance.
(<= (turn_squares (move ?p ?ff ?fr ?tf ?tr) ?ff ?fr ?tf ?tr ?tf ?tr))
(<= (turn_squares (manipulate ?qf ?qr ?ef ?er ?tf ?tr) ?ef ?er ?tf ?tr ?tf ?tr))
(<= (turn_squares (jump_capture ?ff ?fr ?tf ?tr ?jf ?jr) ?ff ?fr ?tf ?tr ?jf ?jr))
(<= (turn_squares (reactive_capture ?bf ?br ?tf ?tr) ?bf ?br ?tf ?tr ?tf ?tr))

(<= (vacated ?move ?f ?r)
    (turn_squares ?move ?f ?r ?tf ?tr ?gf ?gr))
(<= (vacated ?move ?f ?r)
    (turn_squares ?move ?ff ?fr ?tf ?tr ?f ?r))

; A royal that the turn moves stands on the destination ...
(<= (royal_after ?move ?owner ?tf ?tr)
    (turn_squares ?move ?ff ?fr ?tf ?tr ?gf ?gr)
    (royal_at ?owner ?ff ?fr))
; ... and every other royal stays, unless the turn removed it.
(<= (royal_after ?move ?owner ?f ?r)
    (royal_at ?owner ?f ?r)
    (not (vacated ?move ?f ?r)))

(<= (royal_pair_after ?move ?d)
    (royal_after ?move white ?wf ?wr)
    (royal_after ?move black ?bf ?br)
    (manhattan ?wf ?wr ?bf ?br ?d))

(<= (resulting_royal_distance ?move ?d)
    (royal_pair_after ?move ?d)
    (not (closer_royal_pair_after ?move ?d)))
(<= (closer_royal_pair_after ?move ?d)
    (royal_pair_after ?move ?e)
    (distance_less ?e ?d))

; ---- Which turns are captures -------------------------------------------
;
; A capture is exempt from the limit and resets the counts. The turn
; types that can capture while the rule is active (no pawns remain, so
; promotion never happens):
;   - a move onto an occupied square, by any piece, including the king
;     taking a friendly piece or the boulder;
;   - a manipulation that moves the enemy piece onto an occupied square;
;   - the knight's jump-capture and the bishop's reactive capture,
;     which always capture.
(<= (capture_turn (move ?p ?ff ?fr ?tf ?tr))
    (occupied ?tf ?tr))
(<= (capture_turn (manipulate ?qf ?qr ?ef ?er ?tf ?tr))
    (occupied ?tf ?tr))
(<= (capture_turn (jump_capture ?ff ?fr ?tf ?tr ?jf ?jr)))
(<= (capture_turn (reactive_capture ?bf ?br ?tf ?tr)))

(<= (a_capture_turn)
    (turn_made ?move)
    (capture_turn ?move))
(<= (not_a_capture_turn)
    (not (a_capture_turn)))

; ---- Limit: the legal-move filter ---------------------------------------
;
; RULEBOOK: "A player may not make a non-capture turn that would cause
; the count for the resulting royal distance to become greater than 3."
;
; (tiny_endgame_forbids ?move) holds for exactly those turns. Every
; legal rule for a turn that can be a non-capture -- move (boulder
; moves included), transform and manipulate, in steps 1-9 -- ends with
; (not (tiny_endgame_forbids <its move>)), so `legal` itself obeys the
; rule and a GGP player is never offered a forbidden turn. In the step
; files before this one the predicate is undefined and the guard is
; vacuous. jump_capture and reactive_capture always capture, and
; promote / manipulate_promote need a pawn, which the rule's
; activation excludes, so those rules carry no guard.
;
; The loss half of the rule then needs nothing of its own: "If every
; legal turn would do so, that player loses" is the no-legal-turn loss
; of step 6, (lost ?p) <= (control ?p) (not (has_any_legal_turn ?p)),
; applied to the filtered `legal`.
;
; This used to be a separate legal_after_tiny_filter relation whose
; filter, (not (tiny_endgame_limit_exceeded ?next_d)), tested a
; variable never bound to the move. Under negation as failure that
; banned EVERY non-capture turn as soon as ANY distance had count 3,
; whatever distance the turn produced (issue #389).
(<= (tiny_endgame_forbids ?move)
    (true (tiny_endgame_active))
    (resulting_royal_distance ?move ?d)
    (true (distance_count ?d 3))
    (not (capture_turn ?move)))

; ---- Distance count tracking --------------------------------------------
;
; (distance_count ?d ?n), n >= 1: royal distance ?d has occurred ?n
; times while the rule is active. A distance with no fact has count 0,
; as Board.distance_counts holds and as
; cross_validation.board_to_gdl_facts emits it (non-zero counts only).

(<= (resulting_distance_of_turn ?d)
    (turn_made ?move)
    (resulting_royal_distance ?move ?d))

(<= (distance_counted ?d)
    (true (distance_count ?d ?n)))

; After a non-capture turn the count for the RESULTING distance goes up
; by one (from 0 when the distance had no fact) ...
(<= (next (distance_count ?d ?new))
    (true (tiny_endgame_active))
    (not_a_capture_turn)
    (resulting_distance_of_turn ?d)
    (true (distance_count ?d ?old))
    (succ ?old ?new))
(<= (next (distance_count ?d 1))
    (true (tiny_endgame_active))
    (not_a_capture_turn)
    (resulting_distance_of_turn ?d)
    (not (distance_counted ?d)))
; ... and every other count is carried forward unchanged.
(<= (next (distance_count ?d ?n))
    (true (tiny_endgame_active))
    (not_a_capture_turn)
    (true (distance_count ?d ?n))
    (not (resulting_distance_of_turn ?d)))

; After a capture no count is carried forward (all reset to 0), and the
; resulting distance starts again at 1 if the rule still applies.
; (SKETCH: "still applies" is tiny_endgame_position, read before the
; turn; see the activation flag above.)
(<= (next (distance_count ?d 1))
    (true (tiny_endgame_active))
    (a_capture_turn)
    (tiny_endgame_position)
    (resulting_distance_of_turn ?d))

; First activation sets the resulting distance's count to 1. (SKETCH:
; rests on tiny_endgame_position.)
(<= (next (distance_count ?d 1))
    (just_activated)
    (resulting_distance_of_turn ?d))
(<= (just_activated)
    (tiny_endgame_position)
    (not (was_active_last_turn)))

; ---- Carry-over terminal + goals --------------------------------------

(<= terminal (lost white))
(<= terminal (lost black))
(<= (goal white 100) (lost black))
(<= (goal black 100) (lost white))
(<= (goal white 0)   (lost white))
(<= (goal black 0)   (lost black))
